WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.130
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Upper-Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.410
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:15.158
Unit twenty-five: Transport of the Future. In this unit, you will make predictions about transport and cities.

4
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.499
autonomous car.

5
00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:22.068
autonomous car means a car that drives itself without a human driver.

6
00:00:22.368 --> 00:00:25.180
Autonomous cars are being tested in many cities.

7
00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.544
Your turn. Say: autonomous car.

8
00:00:31.244 --> 00:00:32.663
autonomous car.

9
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:34.907
high-speed rail.

10
00:00:35.607 --> 00:00:40.659
high-speed rail means trains that travel at over 250 km per hour.

11
00:00:40.959 --> 00:00:44.341
High-speed rail connects Tokyo and Osaka in two hours.

12
00:00:45.041 --> 00:00:47.635
Your turn. Say: high-speed rail.

13
00:00:50.335 --> 00:00:51.893
high-speed rail.

14
00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:53.792
hyperloop.

15
00:00:54.492 --> 00:00:59.208
hyperloop means a proposed transport system using pods in low-pressure tubes.

16
00:00:59.508 --> 00:01:01.914
The hyperloop could travel faster than a plane.

17
00:01:02.614 --> 00:01:04.778
Your turn. Say: hyperloop.

18
00:01:07.478 --> 00:01:08.398
hyperloop.

19
00:01:09.383 --> 00:01:10.512
electric scooter.

20
00:01:11.212 --> 00:01:14.651
electric scooter means a small electric vehicle you stand on.

21
00:01:14.951 --> 00:01:17.566
Electric scooters are popular with students.

22
00:01:18.266 --> 00:01:21.255
Your turn. Say: electric scooter.

23
00:01:23.955 --> 00:01:25.386
electric scooter.

24
00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:27.396
car sharing.

25
00:01:28.096 --> 00:01:31.616
car sharing means renting cars for short periods from a shared group.

26
00:01:31.916 --> 00:01:34.845
Car sharing reduces the number of cars on the road.

27
00:01:35.545 --> 00:01:37.721
Your turn. Say: car sharing.

28
00:01:40.421 --> 00:01:41.480
car sharing.

29
00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:43.740
congestion charge.

30
00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:48.192
congestion charge means a fee for driving into a busy city centre.

31
00:01:48.492 --> 00:01:51.781
London introduced a congestion charge in 2003.

32
00:01:52.481 --> 00:01:55.203
Your turn. Say: congestion charge.

33
00:01:57.903 --> 00:01:59.252
congestion charge.

34
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:01.158
cycle lane.

35
00:02:01.858 --> 00:02:04.972
cycle lane means a part of the road only for bicycles.

36
00:02:05.272 --> 00:02:08.108
The city built new cycle lanes along the river.

37
00:02:08.808 --> 00:02:11.100
Your turn. Say: cycle lane.

38
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.057
cycle lane.

39
00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.039
flying taxi.

40
00:02:17.739 --> 00:02:22.200
flying taxi means a small electric aircraft carrying passengers in cities.

41
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.731
Flying taxis may appear in some cities within ten years.

42
00:02:26.431 --> 00:02:28.758
Your turn. Say: flying taxi.

43
00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:32.668
flying taxi.

44
00:02:33.683 --> 00:02:35.613
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:35.913 --> 00:02:38.679
Do you think autonomous cars will replace taxis?

46
00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:43.376
They're likely to, but probably not for another twenty years.

47
00:02:44.683 --> 00:02:47.855
What about high-speed rail in Southeast Asia?

48
00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.708
It's bound to expand. Several projects are already planned.

49
00:02:54.017 --> 00:02:55.621
And flying taxis?

50
00:02:56.917 --> 00:03:01.645
They're unlikely to be cheap at first, but cycle lanes and electric scooters will definitely grow.

51
00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.530
Grammar focus: Making predictions.

52
00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:09.037
Use different expressions to show how certain your prediction is.

53
00:03:09.337 --> 00:03:13.705
Bound to means almost certain; likely to means probable; may well means possible.

54
00:03:14.005 --> 00:03:19.453
For example: Traffic is bound to get worse, and electric cars are likely to become cheaper.

55
00:03:19.753 --> 00:03:23.668
These expressions show how sure you are, from almost certain to just possible.

56
00:03:24.683 --> 00:03:28.323
Now read and listen. How Will We Travel in 2050?.

57
00:03:28.623 --> 00:03:33.919
Experts agree that transport is likely to change more in the next thirty years than in the last hundred.

58
00:03:35.217 --> 00:03:38.238
Autonomous cars are bound to become common on motorways.

59
00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:43.488
Many cities may well introduce a congestion charge to reduce traffic.

60
00:03:44.783 --> 00:03:49.163
Cycle lanes and electric scooters are likely to replace short car journeys.

61
00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:54.888
Hyperloops and flying taxis are exciting, but they are unlikely to be cheap at first.

62
00:03:56.183 --> 00:03:58.394
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:58.694 --> 00:04:00.833
A car that drives itself is an blank.

64
00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:05.414
A, autonomous car. B, electric scooter. C, flying taxi.

65
00:04:09.417 --> 00:04:11.544
The answer is A: autonomous car.

66
00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:15.549
Prices blank rise next year; they always do.

67
00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:19.827
A, are bound to. B, are unlikely to. C, may well not.

68
00:04:23.817 --> 00:04:25.491
The answer is A: are bound to.

69
00:04:26.983 --> 00:04:29.740
It's blank to rain today. The sky is clear.

70
00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.939
A, bound. B, likely. C, unlikely.

71
00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.613
The answer is C: unlikely.

72
00:04:40.117 --> 00:04:43.358
A fee for driving into a busy city centre is a blank.

73
00:04:43.658 --> 00:04:47.707
A, cycle lane. B, congestion charge. C, car sharing.

74
00:04:51.717 --> 00:04:54.541
The answer is B: congestion charge.

75
00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:59.234
According to the text, what will replace short car journeys?

76
00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:04.975
A, hyperloops. B, cycle lanes and electric scooters. C, flying taxis.

77
00:05:08.983 --> 00:05:12.051
The answer is B: cycle lanes and electric scooters.

78
00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:18.222
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you think people in your city will travel in 2050?

79
00:05:23.522 --> 00:05:29.911
Most people are likely to use electric vehicles, and the city is bound to build a metro or more cycle lanes.

80
00:05:30.211 --> 00:05:31.711
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:32.717 --> 00:05:36.472
Great work today! You learned eight new words and making predictions.

82
00:05:36.772 --> 00:05:40.864
Today's value is caring for nature. Care for plants, birds and our planet.

83
00:05:41.164 --> 00:05:44.072
See you in Unit twenty-six. Goodbye!

84
00:05:44.372 --> 00:05:47.105
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

